# .env.example
#
# Intention:
#   Catalog of every environment variable the app reads. Copy to `.env` for
#   local development. The real `.env` is gitignored - never commit secrets.
#   `app/config.py` is the single Python-side consumer of these variables.
#
# What this file should contain:
#   - One variable per line in `KEY=value` form.
#   - A short comment above each group explaining what it controls.
#   - Safe placeholder values - empty strings for secrets, dev defaults for URLs.
#
# Example (commented; uncomment and fill in for your project):
#
# # LLM
# LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
#
# # Data stores
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://app:app@db:5432/app
# REDIS_URL=redis://cache:6379/0
# VECTOR_BACKEND=pgvector
#
# # Observability
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO
#
# # MCP - referenced by .mcp.json
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
# SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
# SLACK_TEAM_ID=
# PROJECT_ROOT=.
